type HoverListener = (value: boolean) => void;
const listeners = new Set<HoverListener>();
let current = false;

export function isHoverAllowed(regime: string): boolean {
  return regime === 'atmosphere' || regime === 'surface';
}

/** Pure: hover must auto-disengage (and the toggle refused?) when the regime leaves atmosphere/surface. */
export function hoverDisengages(regime: string, onFoot: boolean): boolean {
  return onFoot || regime === 'space';
}

export function setHoverOn(value: boolean): void { ... }
export function hoverOn(): boolean { return current; }
export function hoverOnSubscribe(fn): () => void { ... }
export function __resetHover(): void { ... }
```

Hmm, wait — should the Space toggle also be refused in space? Per the spec, keyboard Space toggle: "In the atmosphere scheme, the Space keydown toggles the client-side hover state." The atmosphere scheme is active only in the atmosphere regime. In space the scheme is space (no vtol key) so Space does nothing. In the surface scheme… the surface scheme has vtol: null, so Space is the jump key on foot. In the ship + surface regime (docked/landed), the flight loop reads through dockedFlightScheme('surface') = the atmosphere scheme — Space toggles hover. This makes sense: a pad-docked ship, press Space → hover on → the ship lifts off to 10m and hovers.

